84:Tc5a,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a blog?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A blog is a website, or a section of one, that publishes dated articles called posts, usually newest first and in a personal, conversational voice. Cup of Jo and Budget Bytes are blogs. A single article on them is a blog post."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are some good examples of blogs?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It depends on what you want to build. For a personal blog, look at Cup of Jo, Austin Kleon and Zen Habits. For food, Pinch of Yum and Budget Bytes. For a business blog, the Ahrefs, Stripe and HubSpot blogs. For a newsletter, Platformer and Experimental History. The gallery on this page has 60 blog examples you can filter by niche and platform."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What makes a good blog?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A clear topic and a header that shows it, one featured post, categories that work as a menu, a short about box with a face, an email signup that says what readers get, named authors with dates, related posts at the end of each post and one call to action per post. Good blogs also publish on a schedule they can keep."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I start a blog for free?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Pick a free platform, choose a template, write a short about page and publish three to five posts before you share the link. Outrank Blogs is free up to 10,000 visits a month, with no ads and your own domain at no extra cost. WordPress.com, Blogger, Substack and Medium also have free plans, each with different limits."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between a blog and a website?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A website is any set of pages on a domain. A blog is a kind of website, or a part of one, that adds new dated posts over time. Many businesses run both: a website for products and pricing, and a blog at /blog for guides and news, like Stripe, Zapier and Rancho Gordo in the gallery."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many blog posts should I have before launching?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Three to five good posts is enough. That gives a first visitor something to read next and fills your main categories. After launch, a schedule you can keep matters more than a big start."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How often should I post on my blog?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As often as you can publish posts you are proud of. One post a week is a common rhythm for personal and small business blogs. In the gallery, Simon Willison posts every day, while Experimental History says in its sidebar that it publishes every other Tuesday."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which blogging platform do these blogs use?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"31 of the 60 blogs in the gallery run on WordPress. The rest use Substack, Ghost, Shopify, Drupal, Hugo, beehiiv, HubSpot, Craft CMS or their own custom code, and for 6 we could not tell from the page. Use the platform filter in the gallery to see each group."}}]}5c:["$","section",null,{"className":"section ","id":"faq","children":[[["$","script","0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$84"}}]],"$L85"]}]
